behaviors:
- id: detect/answer
  name: brim detect answers with the four margin numbers
  prose: "Given a JPEG picture the tool prints one line of four numbers — margin pixels on the top, bottom, left, and right, each side measured on its own. On the attached bordered.jpg (an even 4-pixel frame) it says 4 4 4 4; on clear.jpg (no margin) it says 0 0 0 0. A search band shallower than the frame cuts the numbers down to the band depth: --band 0.01 gives 2 2 2 2 on the 250-pixel side, because evenness stretches to the end of the band and the whole band is the answer. A deeper one leaves the numbers at the frame: --band 0.05 gives 4 4 4 4, and the stated ceiling --band 0.5 (half the side, no more is allowed) works the same. The threshold knob works across its whole valid range: 0.5 given explicitly matches the default; 0, the least aggressive bar, lets evenness stretch through the whole default band, so the answer is the whole band — 62 pixels, a quarter of the 250-pixel side, and on the non-square clear.jpg a fraction of each side on its own: 87 top and bottom of the 350-pixel height, 127 left and right of the 510-pixel width; 1, the most aggressive, leaves nothing even enough, so no margin is found and the answer is zeros. A repeat run on the same picture prints the same line to the letter."
  scope:
  - main.go
  - picture.go
  - entropy.go
  - margin.go
  - go.mod
  - testdata/bordered.jpg
  - testdata/clear.jpg
  covers:
  - R1
  - R3
  rows:
  - run: ./brim detect testdata/bordered.jpg
    expect:
      rc: 0
      out: |
        4 4 4 4
  - run: ./brim detect testdata/clear.jpg
    expect:
      rc: 0
      out: |
        0 0 0 0
  - run: ./brim detect testdata/bordered.jpg --band 0.01
    expect:
      rc: 0
      out: |
        2 2 2 2
  - run: ./brim detect testdata/bordered.jpg --band 0.05
    expect:
      rc: 0
      out: |
        4 4 4 4
  - run: "a=$(./brim detect testdata/bordered.jpg) && b=$(./brim detect testdata/bordered.jpg) && [ \"$a\" = \"$b\" ] && printf '%s\\n' \"$a\""
    expect:
      rc: 0
      out: |
        4 4 4 4
  - run: ./brim detect testdata/bordered.jpg --threshold 0.5
    expect:
      rc: 0
      out: |
        4 4 4 4
  - run: ./brim detect testdata/bordered.jpg --threshold 0
    expect:
      rc: 0
      out: |
        62 62 62 62
  - run: ./brim detect testdata/bordered.jpg --threshold 1
    expect:
      rc: 0
      out: |
        0 0 0 0
  - run: ./brim detect testdata/clear.jpg --threshold 0
    expect:
      rc: 0
      out: |
        87 87 127 127
  - run: ./brim detect testdata/bordered.jpg --band 0.5
    expect:
      rc: 0
      out: |
        4 4 4 4
- id: detect/knob-refusals
  name: a clumsy invocation is an honest refusal naming the knob and its requirement
  prose: "A bad knob value, a knob without its value, an unknown option, an extra file argument, or no picture at all is refused with exit code 2 and a brief English message on stderr; each invalid knob value is named along with what the knob requires: --band wants a fraction of the side greater than 0 and at most 0.5, --threshold wants a fraction from 0 to 1."
  scope:
  - main.go
  - picture.go
  - testdata/bordered.jpg
  - testdata/clear.jpg
  covers:
  - R1
  rows:
  - run: ./brim
    expect:
      rc: 2
  - run: ./brim detect
    expect:
      rc: 2
  - run: ./brim detect --band abc testdata/bordered.jpg
    expect:
      rc: 2
  - run: ./brim detect --band 0 testdata/bordered.jpg
    expect:
      rc: 2
  - run: ./brim detect --band 0.6 testdata/bordered.jpg
    expect:
      rc: 2
  - run: ./brim detect --threshold 1.5 testdata/bordered.jpg
    expect:
      rc: 2
  - run: ./brim detect --wibble testdata/bordered.jpg
    expect:
      rc: 2
  - run: ./brim detect testdata/bordered.jpg testdata/clear.jpg
    expect:
      rc: 2
- id: detect/picture-troubles
  name: a missing, foreign, or too small picture is reported briefly and clearly
  prose: A missing or unreadable file, a file that is not a JPEG picture, and a picture with a side shorter than two pixels — too small to search for a margin in — are each reported in one brief English line on stderr with exit code 1.
  scope:
  - main.go
  - picture.go
  - testdata/not-jpeg.txt
  - testdata/tiny.jpg
  covers:
  - R1
  rows:
  - run: ./brim detect testdata/missing.jpg
    expect:
      rc: 1
  - run: ./brim detect testdata/not-jpeg.txt
    expect:
      rc: 1
  - run: ./brim detect testdata/tiny.jpg
    expect:
      rc: 1
- id: tool/stack
  name: a Go program on the standard library alone, no third-party dependencies
  prose: "The stack is the customer's demand, not the executor's choice: the tool is a Go program and it uses the standard library only. The module declares no requirements — go.mod carries the single module line and the go directive, nothing else; go list -m all names the main module and nothing but it; and the built binary's own build info contains no dependency line, so no third-party package rides inside the delivered program."
  scope:
  - go.mod
  - build
  - main.go
  - picture.go
  - entropy.go
  - margin.go
  covers:
  - R1
  rows:
  - run: cat go.mod
    expect:
      rc: 0
      out: |
        module brim
        
        go 1.27
  - run: go list -m all
    expect:
      rc: 0
      out: |
        brim
  - run: test -z "$(go version -m ./brim | grep "^dep")" && echo "no third-party dependencies"
    expect:
      rc: 0
      out: |
        no third-party dependencies
- id: tool/purity
  name: the run only reads the picture and prints the answer
  prose: "What must not happen, does not happen: the program writes nothing to disk, goes to no network, keeps no settings in files. A detection run in a scratch directory leaves exactly the one input file it was given, byte-identical to what was copied in, and creates nothing else. A run with a fresh empty HOME leaves that HOME empty — no settings file is ever kept. And the program's whole transitive package closure excludes the net stack, so no network code is even linked into the binary — a socket cannot be opened by code that does not exist."
  scope:
  - main.go
  - picture.go
  - entropy.go
  - margin.go
  - go.mod
  - build
  - testdata/bordered.jpg
  covers:
  - R1
  rows:
  - run: rm -rf .probe && mkdir .probe && cp testdata/bordered.jpg .probe/pic.jpg && ./brim detect .probe/pic.jpg && [ "$(ls -A .probe)" = "pic.jpg" ] && cmp .probe/pic.jpg testdata/bordered.jpg && rm -rf .probe && echo "writes nothing to disk"
    expect:
      rc: 0
      out: |
        4 4 4 4
        writes nothing to disk
  - run: rm -rf .probe-home && mkdir .probe-home && HOME="$PWD/.probe-home" ./brim detect testdata/bordered.jpg && [ -z "$(ls -A .probe-home)" ] && rm -rf .probe-home && echo "keeps no settings in files"
    expect:
      rc: 0
      out: |
        4 4 4 4
        keeps no settings in files
  - run: test -z "$(go list -deps . | grep -x -e net -e net/http)" && echo "no network stack linked"
    expect:
      rc: 0
      out: |
        no network stack linked
